    ],
    "text": "Fish Migration Prediction and Fishery Suggestions"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000009",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "under Marine Environment Changes"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003",
      "p0001-n0012-l0004",
      "p0001-n0012-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The effect of global warming has caused more and more concern all over the world. In particular,  global warming is driving up temperatures in the seas around Scotland, threatening the survival of fish species, including Scotland herring and mackerel. Fish are likely to migrate to the north, where sea temperatures are lower, for better conditions."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We begin with the grey prediction model to predict the sea surface temperature in the next 50 years by combining the historical world greenhouse gas emissions, forest coverage and world population data."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Then, we construct the Marine environment index for both species of fish. We weight the sea surface temperature, the average sea surface salinity and sea depth on different areas of the ocean to get scores of the current environment for the two species. Each species of fish has a preferred range for the environment, which we call the comfort zone."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000",
      "p0001-n0015-l0001",
      "p0001-n0015-l0002",
      "p0001-n0015-l0003",
      "p0001-n0015-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In the fish migration model, we calculate the environment index of the two fish species based on the predicted temperature data. The fish judge the current environment and choose whether to migrate to a more suitable environment. We find that over the next 50 years herring would gradually move to the northeast near Norway, and mackerel will slowly move to the northwest, near Iceland."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0004"
      },
      {
